SUMMARY:Art and Books: Wild Robot: Grades 1-3 at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:The Wild Robot is a beloved children’s book (and now film!) which follows a curious robot called Roz\, who finds herself stranded in the wild on an island. Roz must learn to survive and earn the trust of the island’s animals. This is a beautiful tale of acceptance\, friendship and what it means to care about others. In this workshop for grades 1-3\, we will look at the pen and ink illustrations in the original book and explore themes from the book through various media! Come join us! This is a studio based class with lots of guidance to start followed by one-on-one instruction. Expect to have lots of creative freedom within the bounds of the assignment! \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/art-and-books-wild-robot-grades-1-3-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/03/W2-Robot-01.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Pennsylvania College of Art & Design - Center for Creative Exploration":MAILTO:ce@pcad.edu
END:VEVENT
