SUMMARY:Material Exploration – Sketchbook Creation: Grades 6-9 at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:In this class for students in grades 6-9 we will dive into unconventional art-making by experimenting with a wide range of materials to discover new textures\, forms\, and techniques. Students will explore how different materials behave and be encouraged to push boundaries beyond traditional art supplies and how a sketchbook is the perfect place to experiment. The workshop culminates in creating small mixed-media pieces that reflect each student’s discoveries. This is a studio based class with some guidance to start followed by one-on-one instruction. Expect lots of creative freedom within the bounds of the assignment! \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/material-exploration-sketchbook-creation-grades-6-9-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
